<linker>
  <!--
    link.xml — IL2CPP managed-code preservation rules for the UberStrike mobile build.

    Reasoning:
      * ProjectSettings.asset has `managedStrippingLevel` of 1 (Low) across build
        platforms. The Unity linker walks roots (scenes, build settings, [Preserve]
        attributes, link.xml) and prunes anything else.
      * UberStrike runtime patterns that the linker CANNOT see through:
          1. `Singleton<T>` and `RenderSettingsController` use
             `GetConstructor(BindingFlags.NonPublic)` to invoke private constructors on
             concrete subclass types. The linker sees `T` only as a generic parameter,
             not as the concrete subclasses (BackgroundMusicPlayer, ChatManager,
             AmmoHud, etc.).
          2. Prime31 StoreKit / Etcetera native plugins invoke managed callbacks via
             `UnitySendMessage("StoreKitManager", "productPurchased", json)` —
             dispatched by GameObject name + method-name string, invisible to the linker.
          3. UberStrike.UnitySdk performs serialization via reflection: the
             ExtendableEnum const tables (CmuneDataType / UberStrikeDataType) are read
             with Type.GetFields(). With these stripped, SecureMemory<T>.ReadData fails
             at runtime with "Decode Object failed because found unrecognized datatype"
             ("CmuneSecureVariable failed decrypting Data"). This was the login crash on
             IL2CPP builds.

    Scope:
      * Preserve all of Assembly-CSharp ("preserve all" — broad but safe). Stripping
        savings on this assembly are modest compared to engine code stripping, which
        remains active.
      * Preserve UberStrike.UnitySdk (reflection-based serialization).
      * Preserve P31RestKit (UnitySendMessage callback dispatch; only 16 KB).
      * Preserve System.Linq.Enumerable — LINQ extensions are referenced from generic
        instantiations; without this, IL2CPP may drop Enumerable.Select<int,bool>
        etc. specializations that are referenced only via lambdas.

    Note: Photon3Unity3D.dll was removed from this project ("Photon out, nakama-unity
    in"), so no Photon/AOT rules are needed; the rebuilt SDK no longer uses
    MakeGenericType-based dictionary deserialization.
  -->

  <assembly fullname="Assembly-CSharp" preserve="all" />

  <assembly fullname="UberStrike.UnitySdk" preserve="all" />

  <assembly fullname="P31RestKit" preserve="all" />

  <assembly fullname="System.Core">
    <type fullname="System.Linq.Enumerable" preserve="all" />
  </assembly>
</linker>
